{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "bike-repair-desk",
  "title": "Bike Repair Desk",
  "summary": "A puncture repair needs a tube and rim tape. Write the estimate the customer will see before they approve the repair.",
  "className": "RepairDesk",
  "starter": "class RepairDesk:\n    def __init__(self):\n        pass\n\n    def open_estimate(self, ticket, bike, shop, labor_cents):\n        pass\n\n    def set_part(self, ticket, sku, units, unit_cents):\n        pass\n\n    def view(self, ticket):\n        pass\n",
  "levels": [
    {
      "title": "Write the estimate",
      "requirements": "At the Canal counter, a mechanic has found damaged rim tape inside a wheel with a flat tire. The customer wants the full price before they leave the bike.\n\nStart with no tickets. The two shop IDs are \"canal\" and \"station\". Ticket numbers, bike descriptions, and part SKUs are nonempty ASCII strings. Compare strings as written. Quantities and prices are integers. Prices are in cents.\n\nopen_estimate(ticket, bike, shop, labor_cents) creates an estimate and returns True. Return False if the ticket number already exists, the shop is unknown, or labor_cents is negative. A new estimate has no parts.\n\nset_part(ticket, sku, units, unit_cents) sets the quoted quantity and price for that SKU. A second call for the same SKU replaces the whole line. Zero units removes the line if it exists. Return True for an accepted edit, including removal of an absent line. Return False if the ticket is missing, its status is not \"estimate\", or either number is negative.\n\nview(ticket) returns None for an unknown ticket. Otherwise, return a new dictionary with these keys.\n- \"bike\" and \"shop\" hold the stored strings.\n- \"status\" is \"estimate\" when you open the ticket.\n- \"parts\" is a list of [sku, units, unit_cents] lists sorted by SKU in ascending order.\n- \"total_cents\" is the labor price plus the sum of units times unit_cents for the quoted parts.\n\nA rejected call changes nothing. The tests supply arguments of the stated types.",
      "visible": [
        {
          "id": "canal-puncture-estimate",
          "kind": "requirements",
          "steps": [
