    {
      "title": "Set parts aside",
      "requirements": "Two customers just approved quotes that need the last nine-speed chain at Canal. Reserve the chain for the first ticket that can take it. Each shop has its own shelf stock.\n\nBoth shops start with zero stock. An estimate reserves nothing. Keep the estimate methods from the previous level.\n\nreceive(shop, sku, units) adds units to the shop's physical stock and returns True. Return False for an unknown shop or a quantity of zero or less.\n\nstock(shop, sku) returns [on_hand, available]. on_hand is the quantity physically present. available is on_hand minus the quantity reserved by approved tickets at that shop. A known shop with no units of the SKU returns [0, 0]. Return None for an unknown shop.\n\napprove(ticket) accepts a ticket in \"estimate\" status only. Check the available quantity of every quoted part at its shop. When all parts are available, reserve those quantities, set the status to \"approved\", and return True. An estimate with no parts can be approved. If the ticket is missing or has the wrong status, or any part is short, return False. A failed approval reserves nothing and leaves the ticket unchanged.\n\nAn approved quote keeps the labor price and parts you saw before approval. set_part still accepts only estimates.",
