    {
      "title": "Close the ticket",
      "requirements": "The mechanic fitted the reserved pads on one bike. A different customer canceled before work started. The first ticket uses up its parts. The other ticket puts its reserved parts back on the available shelf.\n\ncomplete(ticket) closes an approved ticket and returns its quoted total in cents. Subtract the reserved units from physical stock at the ticket's shop, clear its reservation, and set its status to \"completed\". Return None if the ticket is missing or its status is not \"approved\". An approved free job closes with a return value of 0.\n\ncancel(ticket) cancels a ticket in \"estimate\" or \"approved\" status and returns True. If approved, clear its reservation without changing physical stock. Set its status to \"canceled\". Return False if the ticket is missing, completed, or already canceled.\n\nCompleted and canceled tickets stay in the records. view shows their new status and original quote. They cannot be approved, edited, or opened again under the same number.",
